M6	Content	Integrations	GenAI tool definitions	the attribute gen_ai.tool.definitions
M6	Content	Integrations	GenAI input messages	the attribute gen_ai.input.messages
M6	Content	Integrations	GenAI output messages	the attribute gen_ai.output.messages
M6	Content	Integrations	GenAI tool call arguments	the attribute gen_ai.tool.call.arguments
M6	Content	Integrations	GenAI tool call result	the attribute gen_ai.tool.call.result
M6	Content	Integrations	GenAI memory records	the attribute gen_ai.memory.records
M6	Content	Integrations	GenAI retrieval documents	the attribute gen_ai.retrieval.documents
M7	Content	Integrations	relations	every row of a relation draws on the same domains
M7	Content	Integrations	GenAI structured attributes	the fields of the eight; every object allows further properties
M8	Content	Integrations	relations	a domain may be nonsimple: its elements are relations
M8	Content	Integrations	relations	normalization: each subordinate relation takes its parent's primary key, and the parent's nonsimple domains are struck out
M8	Content	Integrations	relations	normalization applies when the nesting is a tree and no primary key is nonsimple
M8	Content	Integrations	JSON Pointer	reference tokens, each prefixed by '/'; in a token '~' is written '~0' and '/' is written '~1'
M9	Content	Integrations	OTLP records	a span is identified by trace id and span id; a log record carries them only optionally
M9	Content	Integrations	JSON Pointer	a string that identifies a specific value within a JSON document
M9	Content	Integrations	relations	normalization: each subordinate relation takes its parent's primary key, and the parent's nonsimple domains are struck out
M10	Content	Integrations	JSON Pointer	a string that identifies a specific value within a JSON document
M10	Content	Integrations	JSON	a value is false, null, true, an object, an array, a number or a string
M11	Content	Integrations	relations	the ordering of rows is immaterial
M11	Content	Integrations	JSON	an array is an ordered sequence
M11	Content	Integrations	JSON Pointer	a token names an object member, or an array element by its zero-based index
M11	Content	Integrations	GenAI input messages	in the order sent to the model
M12	Content	Integrations	relations	a domain may be nonsimple: its elements are relations
M12	Content	Integrations	relations	a relation whose domains are all simple is a two-dimensional array
M13	Content	Integrations	GenAI structured attributes	the fields of the eight; every object allows further properties
M14	Content	Integrations	JSON	an implementation may limit the range and precision of numbers
M15	Content	Format	sheet names and fields	holding HT, LF, FF or CR: cannot be represented, and a generator does not write them
M16	Content	Integrations	OTLP JSON	keys are the lowerCamelCase field names
M16	Content	Integrations	JSON Pointer	a string that identifies a specific value within a JSON document
M16	Content	Integrations	JSON	a value is false, null, true, an object, an array, a number or a string
M16	Content	Integrations	GenAI structured attributes	the fields of the eight; every object allows further properties
M16	Content	Integrations	relations	normalization: each subordinate relation takes its parent's primary key, and the parent's nonsimple domains are struck out
M17	Content	Integrations	OTLP records	a span is identified by trace id and span id; a log record carries them only optionally
M17	Content	Integrations	relations	normally a domain, or a combination of domains, uniquely identifies each row: the primary key
M18	Content	Format	sheets	a sheet is a header and an ordered sequence of zero or more records; an MTSV file is an ordered sequence of sheets
M19	Content	Format	fields	a field is text
M19	Content	Format	empty fields	by default a cell whose string value is empty has the value null; the model does not tell an empty value from a quoted empty one
M19	Content	Integrations	GenAI structured attributes	the fields of the eight; every object allows further properties
